<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Lisbon (1668)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1668">1668</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-restoration-war">Portuguese Restoration War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> was signed on 13 February 1668 between Portugal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> with English mediation. By it Spain recognised the independence of Portugal and the rule of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-braganza">House of Braganza</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-restoration-war">Portuguese Restoration War</a> that had begun in 1640. Portugal in turn recognised Spanish possession of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A revolt on 1 December 1640 placed the Duke of Braganza on the throne as John IV, and Spain recognised independence by the <b>Treaty of Lisbon</b> in 1668.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-portugal">Kingdom of Portugal · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The Restoration War ended with Spanish recognition of Portuguese independence in the <b>Treaty of Lisbon</b> of 1668.</blockquote><a href="/state/iberian-union">Iberian Union</a></li></ul></section>
